cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "qcrispr: set-level CRISPR guide selection with bulge-aware off-target scoring"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the datasets it evaluates on. See NOTICE."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Livia
repository-code: "https://github.com/LiviaChowdary/qcrispr"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Guide-RNA selection for multiplex CRISPR editing, posed as a quadratic binary
  optimisation problem over a set of guides rather than a per-guide ranking,
  with bulge-aware off-target enumeration and scoring. Reports AUPR 0.4274 with
  a bootstrap interval of 0.341 to 0.522 on the refined TrueOT benchmark,
  trained on CHANGE-seq and fine-tuned on cellular GUIDE-seq with all benchmark
  guides excluded from training. Includes a comparison against the published
  CFD score on matched folds, which the existing benchmark literature omits,
  and a negative result on QAOA for the selection problem.
keywords:
  - CRISPR
  - off-target prediction
  - guide RNA design
  - combinatorial optimisation
  - QAOA
